{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>To say: In the fifth month</b> — He mentioned this fast because the House was burned on the tenth of the fifth month. And let there be no doubt in your heart, for you will find that it was burned on the seventh of the month, for the explanation is that its edge was burned, and Jerusalem was destroyed a second time in the days of Titus on the ninth of Av, and it is for that second destruction that we fast." "<b>Should I separate myself</b> — That they should separate themselves from all delicacies and food, but only weep. And behold, the priests did not know how to answer, for this fast is not written in the Torah, but they took it upon themselves when they saw the destruction of the First House. And behold, the prophet prophesied and answered at the end of the passage."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The argument is compressed: Ibn Ezra addresses an apparent contradiction between sources dating the burning to the 7th versus the 10th of the fifth month. 'Its edge was burned' (קצהו) is hyper-literal; the syntax is obscure but rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:14.951601133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}